ies on the occasion of killing the mighty Asura Vſtra.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-25-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2022013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6143e08f65a59eda5cdf93937bd42814cabc26a1450a208da62e29c6a57a8073","compact":"4a2664e6d0c2f7eb5e68110049c28b04295a378c86c748fde8cb9e007c87099b","nasal":"a54cefd84b9b1500eb82304304fa7ffe337afcd3a67a4e62203b1182db9e1423"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-22-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":22,"verse":14,"english":"May that blessing attend you, which was invoked in olden times by Vinatā, for that king of birds Garuda, praying for nectar.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-25-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2022014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"53e24f4637464c2b11ab0b58fb0bf0fa6b445f01cbbd95cf154683437cbfdf38","compact":"2511d55c5e1c19be57aaf305fcbffc002a6e2171b15528df648605640cbcc66a","nasal":"47e0a7cd6f7f94c653df5c994f450c8a2b81dc2323198ac8d4bab6a7f179cdbe"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-22-15","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":22,"verse":15,"english":"Saying this Kausalyā, the foremost of all women, having expansive eyes, placed the grains on Rāma's head; sprinkled his body with fragrant substances, and tied to his hands, as amulet, twigs of such auspicious plants as Viśalyakaraṇī, with due mental repetition of mantras.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.726,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-25-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2022015","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1509010860dedbff9eabf01116323212b37cc939fed3c57e4e2450c3ab2d14a1","compact":"9b80f037912cde95c83a89ede8ec4c828ef64440c84113eabc04cc1e361c5