h Rāghava, contribute to your welfare, who are going to the forest for a long time.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.721,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-25-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2022018","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"11c2aa7662696b821cdba26fe9afe835514093dabbe74c3057486583561359c5","compact":"5a1d694e2a3fb34a2fe8693ba0f37ea0ada65c0f35f3ff4ff020f9e87ea6c2bb","nasal":"24530b9c0a2433c4362ed692d2cd2b3333b7144b93a7ee75045b766b48589f7b"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-22-19","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":22,"verse":19,"english":"Kausalya, having her eyes full of tears, and performing the benedictory ceremonies with due rites, went round Rāghava with solemnity, and seeing him again and again sighed hot and hard.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.78,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-25-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2022019","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ffa4f301ea2b84a80d5c67f45a21900863a3cfcbe0652d7b1de2b465732008eb","compact":"5ad91edd0b523cfa5677e85cb640d2711f78076d0d0eacbff21255ef8d37b599","nasal":"5ad91edd0b523cfa5677e85cb640d2711f78076d0d0eacbff21255ef8d37b599"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-22-20","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":22,"verse":20,"english":"Being gone round by his mother thus, Rāghava, of great lame, and resplendent with the splendour of beauty, proceeded towards the abode of Sītā, after bowing down to the feet of his mother repeatedly.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.744,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-25-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2022020","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8c75cc98b88cb161eaed9a6f3eb5b35177d71b1ca3a7feea66ba4c90b01e74a1","compact":"852281cdaec2808679aea11bb5daddf06ff25947e6